.TH JOBWRAP.TOML 5 "August 2026" "jobwrap 0.1" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
jobwrap.toml \- jobwrap configuration file
.SH DESCRIPTION
The jobwrap configuration lives at \fI~/.config/jobwrap/config.toml\fR.
\fBconfig_version = 1\fR is required. Unknown fields are rejected.
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B [server]
\fBbind\fR (default 127.0.0.1), \fBport\fR (default 8765),
\fBpublic_base_url\fR, \fBopen_browser_on_start\fR, \fBallow_remote_bind\fR
(default false).
.TP
.B [daemon]
\fBauto_start\fR (default true), \fBidle_shutdown_minutes\fR (default 0).
.TP
.B [defaults]
\fBprofile\fR, \fBallocate_pty\fR, \fBrecord_output\fR,
\fBretain_completed_days\fR, \fBmaximum_log_bytes\fR, \fBshow_job_url\fR,
\fBjob_name_template\fR.
.TP
.B [authentication]
\fBtrust_local_owner\fR, \fBbrowser_session_minutes\fR,
\fBpassword_attempt_limit\fR, \fBpassword_attempt_window_seconds\fR.
.TP
.B [profiles.NAME]
Access fields: \fBstatus\fR, \fBoutput\fR, \fBcommand\fR,
\fBworking_directory\fR, \fBsend_input\fR, \fBsignal_interrupt\fR,
\fBsignal_terminate\fR, \fBsignal_stop\fR, \fBsignal_continue\fR,
\fBsignal_kill\fR, \fBrestart\fR, \fBdelete\fR.
.SH ACCESS LEVELS
Each access field accepts one of:
.RS
.IP public
Anyone.
.IP authenticated
Any session or token.
.IP controller
A logged-in browser session, or a token with a matching grant.
.IP owner
The local Unix user who launched the job.
.IP disabled
Nobody.
.RE
.PP
Public output may itself contain secrets; use the private profile for
sensitive work.
.SH PRECEDENCE
Built-in defaults, user configuration, named profile, trusted project
configuration, environment, then command-line options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR jobwrap (1)
